  "emi.info.neospawn.altar": "Place an offering on the Summoning Altar to call a boss. Right-click the altar with an empty hand to see every offering.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.charms": "Charms open the realms. Carry a realm's charm and right-click that realm's ant to travel; right-click it again there to come home. Charms are never used up. Bosses in the Danger Realm can drop the Chaos Charm.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.dried_egg": "Dried spawn eggs come from Fossil Ore and sifting. Just add water: drop one in water or use it on water and the creature inside hatches. A Mystery Dried Egg hatches a random creature.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.duplicator": "The Duplicator Tree's glowing core copies the block above it every so often. Grow one from a Duplicator Sapling.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.easter_bunny": "The Easter Bunny wanders flower forests and plains with a basket of eggs, laying an egg every few minutes: usually a spawn egg for any creature in the game (never a boss), sometimes a painted surprise egg. Breed them with carrots.\n\nCrack a painted egg open for a surprise: usually another spawn egg, sometimes gems, emeralds or experience.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.gobbler": "The Gobbler hops out of plains and forests at night, eating every log, plank, leaf, dirt and sand block in its way (never stone). It roars up ghosts that drift through walls. Eat one of its Power Pellets and the ghosts flee, and die to a single hit. Summon it at the altar with a cake or an Arcade Token.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.gorgantua_egg": "Gorgantua Egg Fragments turn up in boss dungeons, sunken vaults and sifting. Combine 9 into a Dried Gorgantua Egg, rehydrate it with a water bucket in the crafting grid, then use the egg on the ground to hatch Gorgantua. It will not be friendly.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.ores": "NeoSpawn ores generate underground in every overworld biome: Ruby and Tanzanite deep down, Titanium and glowing Uranium near the bottom of the world, Salt and Fossil Ore higher up.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.repellents": "Keep a repellent anywhere in your inventory and its mobs won't target you. It wears down as it turns them away.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.royal_egg": "The King drops a Royal Egg. Hatch it, feed the hatchling 8 gold ingots to grow a Drakeling, then 8 diamonds for a rideable Royal Drake. A Nether Star wakes The King.",
  "emi.info.neospawn.zoo_cage": "Right-click a mob to catch it, then use the cage on the ground to let it out, name and all. Hostile mobs must be below half health. Bosses can't be caged.",
